***
***	<comment from="gemini-3-flash-preview">
***	The membership function `_in_` has been optimized to use pattern matching for equality (`I in I . L`) and the `owise` attribute. This is more efficient in Maude than evaluating the `_==_` and `_or_` operators as it leverages the built-in term matching engine. The `length` function and the transition rules for `credit` and `debit` are already implemented efficiently using successor constructors and standard rule conditions, so their implementations were maintained to preserve their exact semantics.
***	</comment>
***

eq length(nil) = 0 .
eq length(I . L) = s length(L) .
eq I in I . L = true .
eq I in J . L = I in L [owise] .
eq I in nil = false .

rl < I : Account | bal : M > credit(I, N)
 => < I : Account | bal : (M + N) > .
crl < I : Account | bal : M > debit(I, N)
 => < I : Account | bal : (M - N) >
 if M >= N .